                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar \partial_E \colon \Gamma(E)\longrightarrow \Gamma(E) \otimes_{C^\infty(X, \mathbb{C})}\Omega^{0,1}(X)
            %p
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ∂
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ∂
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \partial_E \circ \bar \partial_E = 0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+operator"} Dolbeault operator
            %p
              The analogous statement is true for generalization of vector bundles to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+sheaves"} module sheaves
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+cohomology"} coherent cohomology
          %p
            (For a discussion on this use of the terminology “holomorphically flat”, see
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/236370/confusion-surrounding-the-koszul-malgrange-theorem"} this MO question
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+varieties"} complex varieties
            this statement is due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            and (
            %a{:href => "#KoszulMalgrange58"}> Koszul-Malgrange 58
            ), recalled for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Pali06"}> Pali 06, theorem 1
            ). It may be understood as a special case of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Newlander-Nirenberg+theorem"} Newlander-Nirenberg theorem
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#DelzantPy10"} Delzant-Py 10, section 6
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifold"} infinite-dimensional
            vector bundles. Over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#OverRiemannSurfaces"} below
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahBott83"} Atiyah-Bott 83
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan-Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan-Seshadri theorem
          %p
            As an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            and with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            generalized to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            the statement appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Pali06"}> Pali 06
            ). This is generalized to an equivalence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+chain+complexes"} categories of chain complexes
            of coherent sheaves, hence to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi D
                    %mi coh
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{coh}^b(X)
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+cohomology"} coherent cohomology
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Block05"} Block 05, theorem 4.1.3
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The equivalence in theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KoszulMalgrangeTheorem"}
              serves to relate a fair bit of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
              with constructions in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobians"} intermediate Jacobians
              arise in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
              as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+flat+connections"} moduli spaces of flat connections
              equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              directly comes down
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
              (and/or some variants of that, under the exponential exact sequence).
          %p We state the derived version in more detail:
          #ChainComplexesOfHolomorphicFlatConnections.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi hol
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
