                  are the evident
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
                  (…).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Block05"}> Block 05, def. 2.3.2 in theorem 4.1.3
            ).
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi hol
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi D
                      %mi coh
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho Rep(T_{hol}X) \simeq D^b_{coh}(X)
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
              of complexes of holomorphic flat connections, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChainComplexesOfHolomorphicFlatConnections"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+sheaves"} module sheaves
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+cohomology"} coherent cohomology
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Block05"}> Block 05, theorem 4.1.3
            ).
          %h2#related_theorems Related theorems
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan-Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan-Seshadri theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau+theorem"} Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kobayashi-Hitchin+correspondence"} Kobayashi-Hitchin correspondence
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The classical statement of theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KoszulMalgrangeTheorem"}
            is due (according to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Pali06"} Pali 06
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            and
          %ul
            %li#KoszulMalgrange58
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Koszul"}> Jean-Louis Koszul
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+Malgrange"} Bernard Malgrange
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sur certaine structures fibrées complexes
          %p
            Over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            and in the context of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connections"} moduli space of flat connections
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahBott83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"} Raoul Bott
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Yang-Mills equations over Riemann surfaces
              %p
                Vol. 308, No. 1505 (Mar. 17, 1983), pp. 523-615 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/37156"}> jstor
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/a/295505/58526"} lighning summary
            %li#Evans
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Evans"}> Jonathan Evans
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahjde/yangmills.htm"} Aspects of Yang-Mills theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahjde/YM-lectures/lecture10.pdf"} lecture 10
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahjde/YM-lectures/lecture11.pdf"} lecture 11
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahjde/YM-lectures/lecture12.pdf"} lecture 12
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Pali06
              N. Pali,
              %em
                Faisceaux
                = succeed "-cohrents" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo ∂
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \partial
              (
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \partial
                \-Coherent sheaves on complex manifolds) Math. Ann. 336 (2006), no. 3, 571–615 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0305422"}> arXiv:math/0305422
                )
          %p
            Further Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of holomorphic vector bundles is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Block05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Block"}> Jonathan Block
              ,
              %em Duality and equivalence of module categories in noncommutative geometry I
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0509284"}> arXiv:0509284
              )
          %p
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-algebroid+representations"} Lie infinity-algebroid representations
            of the holomorphic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifold"} infinite-dimensional
            vector bundles is in
          %ul
            %li#DelzantPy10
              Thomas Delzant, Pierre Py,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kähler groups, real hyperbolic spaces and the Cremona group
              = succeed ")" do
